# Arguments of feosd (feosd.service). For example, to serve the API on TCP
# too, without authentication, for a lab:
#
#   FEOSD_ARGS="--tcp [::]:1337"
#
# Pods have an IPv6 address on the network and an IPv4 address for
# leaving this node through masquerade (ADR 0010). feosd needs the prefix
# that the network routes to this node to give pods a network; without it,
# pods with a network fail:
#
#   --pod-prefix PREFIX       e.g. 2001:db8:7:1::/64. A /64 is best, a
#                             smaller one such as a /80 is enough. A lab
#                             whose network routes nothing to the node takes
#                             a ULA, such as fd00:fe05:1::/64: its pods leave
#                             over IPv4 alone, and nothing outside the node
#                             reaches them.
#   --pod-ipv4-range PREFIX   the pods' IPv4 addresses, a /32 each,
#                             169.254.16.0/20 by default.
#   --dns-address ADDRESS     the pods' resolver, an IPv4 address this node
#                             holds, 169.254.0.53 by default. Pods' gateway
#                             is 169.254.0.1, which the node answers ARP for
#                             on their TAP devices and never holds.
#   --dns-upstream ADDRESS    a resolver it asks for pods that name none
#                             (repeatable); Google's and Cloudflare's by
#                             default.
#   --deny-prefix PREFIX      a prefix of either family that no pod reaches
#                             (repeatable): the control plane, management
#                             networks. Link-local addresses, such as a
#                             cloud's metadata service, and this node's own
#                             are denied always.
#
# A lab:
#
#   FEOSD_ARGS="--pod-prefix fd00:fe05:1::/64 --deny-prefix 10.0.0.0/8"
FEOSD_ARGS=""
